add(45,'Brown Apple Sauce with Gravy',8,35,'Apples simmer in brown gravy and are mashed into a savory sauce with a small cayenne finish.',[A(6),I('gravy',250,'ml','ready-to-serve low-sodium brown beef gravy','Use 250 ml ready-to-serve vegetable gravy for a meat-free variation.'),I('cayenne',.125,'tsp','ground cayenne pepper','Omit for a mild sauce.')],['Peel and core {{apples}} and cut into small pieces. Put them in a heavy saucepan with {{gravy}}.','Cover and simmer gently for 20–25 minutes, stirring often, until the apples are soft. Add a small splash of water if the gravy begins to catch.','Mash until smooth and stir in {{cayenne}}. Heat until piping hot and serve.'],'Ready-to-serve gravy resolves the missing component without requiring a separate recipe. The source half-pint becomes a modern 250 ml choice.','Sauces')
add(34,'Alma-Mártás (Creamy Savory Apple Sauce)',6,35,'Tart apples soften in butter, then thicken a light stock sauce finished with lemon and cream.',[A(3),B(20),I('flour',8,'g','all-purpose flour','Use 8 g a gluten-free flour blend suitable for sauces; texture may differ.'),I('stock',150,'ml','unsalted beef stock','Use 150 ml unsalted vegetable stock for a meat-free variation.'),Z(2),L(10),S(15),cream(30)],['Peel and core {{apples}} and slice thinly. Melt {{butter}} in a saucepan, add the apples and cook gently for 8–10 minutes, stirring, until beginning to soften.','Sprinkle in {{flour}} and stir over low heat for 2 minutes without burning. Gradually stir in {{stock}}.','Add {{zest}}, {{lemon}} and {{sugar}}. Simmer for 8–10 minutes, stirring, until the apples are tender and the sauce lightly thickened.','Stir in {{cream}}, bring just to a gentle simmer and serve.'],'Three apples are selected from the source two-or-three range. Missing quantities and cooking cues are supplied. Unsalted stock is used; the optional commercial meat extract is omitted from the base.','Sauces')
