add(24,'Sweet Apple Sauce with Brandy',10,50,'Smooth apple sauce receives cinnamon, lemon and a generous brandy finish for serving with desserts.',[A(6),W(500),L(10),S(227),C(1),I('brandy',120,'ml','brandy','Use 120 ml unsweetened apple juice for an alcohol-free variation; flavor differs.')],['Peel and core {{apples}}, cut into pieces and put in a saucepan with {{water}} and {{lemon}}. Simmer for 25–30 minutes until very soft.','Press through a sieve into a clean pan. Stir in {{sugar}} and {{cinnamon}} until dissolved.','Take the pan off the heat before adding {{brandy}}. Return to low heat and simmer gently for 5 minutes, stirring; do not ignite the alcohol. Serve warm.'],'The source gill is assigned 120 ml and pint 500 ml as modern choices. This brandy version is not alcohol-free after a short simmer.','Sauces')
