add(4,'Meissen-Style Apple Sauce with Sour Cream',8,115,'Smooth cooked apples are flavored with cinnamon and lemon, then cooled and mixed with sour cream.',[A(4),S(40),C(.25),Z(2),W(60),I('sour',150,'g','sour cream','Use 150 g full-fat plain yogurt for a lighter, tangier sauce.')],['Peel and core {{apples}}, cut into small pieces and put in a saucepan with {{sugar}}, {{cinnamon}}, {{zest}} and {{water}}.','Cover and simmer for 15–25 minutes, stirring, until very soft. Press through a sieve.','Transfer to a shallow container, cool briefly and refrigerate within 2 hours. Once cold, stir in {{sour}} and serve chilled.'],'A measured stovetop method replaces the unclear baking-sheet stewing instruction. Sour cream is set at 150 g because the source deciliter/spoon wording conflicts; this is a modern choice, not a recovered conversion. The optional wine sauce requires a separate formulation and is not silently equated with sour cream.','Sauces')
add(47,'Chilled Apple Sauce Mould',6,280,'Sweetened smooth apple sauce is set with gelatin into a soft fruit mould for serving cold.',[I('apples',500,'g','peeled and cored cooking apples','Use the same prepared weight of another cooking apple.'),W(80),W(60,'bloomwater'),S(50),I('gelatin',10,'g','unflavored powdered gelatin','Use the same weight and strength of another powdered gelatin; vegetarian gelling agents are not direct replacements.')],['Cut {{apples}} into small pieces and simmer with {{water}} for 15–20 minutes until very soft, stirring to prevent catching. Mash thoroughly or sieve.','Sprinkle {{gelatin}} evenly over {{bloomwater}} in a bowl and leave for 5 minutes to hydrate.','Stir {{sugar}} into the hot apple puree. Remove from the heat and stir in the hydrated gelatin until completely dissolved; do not boil after adding gelatin.','Spoon into a lightly water-rinsed 750 ml mould, or individual dishes. Cool briefly, cover and refrigerate for at least 4 hours until set. Dip the outside briefly in warm water to unmould, or serve in the dishes.'],'Gelatin strength and fruit moisture vary; 10 g is an explicit modern setting amount rather than an exact tablespoon conversion. The total time includes chilling.')
add(13,'Appelspijs Gebakken (Baked Apple and Egg Batter)',8,115,'Apple cubes and currants bake in an egg-rich batter scented with cinnamon and lemon.',[A(4),I('flour',80,'g','all-purpose flour','Use 80 g a gluten-free all-purpose baking blend; texture may differ.'),W(120),I('eggs',8,'','large eggs','Use 400 g pasteurized liquid whole egg; an egg-free substitute needs a different recipe.'),S(100),C(1),Z(2),I('currants',60,'g','dried currants','Use 60 g raisins, chopped if large.'),B(25)],['Heat the oven to 160°C (320°F). Use {{butter}} to grease a deep 23 cm baking dish. Peel and core {{apples}} and cut into 2 cm cubes.','Whisk {{flour}} with {{water}} until smooth. Beat in {{eggs}}, {{sugar|0.8}}, {{cinnamon|0.5}} and {{zest}}, then fold in {{currants}} and the apple cubes.','Pour into the prepared dish. Bake for 75–90 minutes until the center is set and reaches at least 71°C (160°F); cover loosely if the surface browns too soon.','Rest for 10 minutes. Mix the remaining {{sugar|0.2}} and {{cinnamon|0.5}} and sprinkle over before serving.'],'The source eight eggs and long gentle bake remain. Flour, water, fruit, sugar and pan size are supplied to define the previously incomplete batter. Temperature is a modern choice.')
add(30,'Two-Texture Apple Compote',6,70,'Whole poached apples sit beneath a sauce made by cooking a second portion of apples down in the same lemon syrup.',[A(6),S(227),W(180),L(15),Z(2),I('nutmeg',.125,'tsp','ground nutmeg','Omit or use the same small volume of cinnamon.'),I('icing',10,'g','powdered sugar','Omit for a less sweet finish.')],['Peel and core {{apples|0.5}}, keeping them whole. Peel, core and chop the remaining {{apples|0.5}}.','Heat {{sugar}}, {{water}}, {{lemon}} and {{zest}} in a snug saucepan until the sugar dissolves. Add the whole apples, cover and simmer gently for 20–35 minutes until tender, turning and basting carefully. Add a little water if needed to keep the syrup fluid. Lift onto a dish.','Add the chopped apples to the syrup and simmer for 15–20 minutes until they collapse. Mash or press through a sieve to make a smooth coating sauce.','Spoon over the whole apples and sprinkle with {{nutmeg}} and {{icing}}. Serve warm, or cool promptly and refrigerate.'],'The source dozen is halved, interpreting its six intact apples and six sauce apples as equal portions. Extra starting water is a modern adjustment to reduce scorching while retaining the two textures.')
